      },
      "id": 1,
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "indexByName": {
              "building": 0,
              "floor": 1,
              "room": 2,
              "pct_ok": 3,
              "pct_alarm": 4,
              "t_mean": 5,
              "t_min": 6,
              "t_max": 7,
              "h_mean": 8,
              "h_min": 9,
              "h_max": 10,
              "mould_h": 11,
              "twpi": 12,
              "coverage_d": 13
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About these metrics",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Reading this report**\n\n- **Time in range**: share of 15-minute intervals with status OK. Aim for 95 % or more.\n- **TWPI** (time-weighted preservation index): estimated years until paper and other organic materials show noticeable chemical decay at these conditions. About 45 years at 68 °F / 50 % RH. Above 75 is good, 45–75 is acceptable, below 45 means faster ageing. Cooler and drier raises it. (Sebera isoperm method, approximate IPI equivalent.)\n- **Hours RH > 65 %**: mould germination risk rises with time above 65 % RH, and sharply after about 48 continuous hours.\n- **Data (days)**: amount of data the row is based on. Low values mean the sensor was offline or newly installed.\n\nTo print or save as PDF, use the browser's print function in kiosk view (add `?kiosk` to the address)."
      },
      "id": 2
    }
  ]
}